          src: "/diagrams/NG-GER-0595.svg",
          alt: "Falls in old age — why they happen and how to prevent them: a fall is several small problems arriving at the same moment. Within the person: poor vision and cataract, weak legs and unsteady gait, dizziness on standing, confusion or dementia, foot pain and poor footwear, urgency to reach the toilet, a previous fall — the strongest single predictor of the next. In the medicines: sedatives and sleeping tablets, antihypertensives, diuretics, antipsychotics, antidiabetic drugs causing hypos, anything newly started; four or more medicines sharply raises risk. In the home: loose mats and trailing cloth, wet or polished floors, poor light and no light at night, steps without a handrail, latrine far from the house, uneven compound and open gutter, clutter. After a fall ask why it happened, not only whether something is broken. The hidden injury is fear: the person stops walking, muscles weaken and the next fall becomes more likely; restricting activity is not a safety measure. What works: strength and balance exercise, review and reduce the medicine list, treat vision, check lying and standing blood pressure.",
